# The reviewer /ship runs for step 7, the security pass. Two shapes: agent:<name>
# dispatches that agent on this host, and anything else is a command line the
# audit prompt is appended to.
#
# `auto` means the shape is chosen when the gate runs: the security-reviewer
# agent when a definition for it is on this host or in the project, otherwise
# Claude Code with Fable in plan mode. With neither one there the gate stops and
# names this file rather than running nothing.
#
# The probe reads agent definition files, so an agent that arrives through a
# plugin is invisible to it. On such a host write agent:security-reviewer here;
# an explicit value is never probed. An explicit agent: value on a host that
# cannot dispatch agents still stops the gate rather than running something else.
#
# Copy this file to config/security-reviewer to change it: /ship reads config/
# first and falls back here.
auto
